  "about": "The hunt ladder's typed tables (tools/src/balance/hunt-ladder.ts reads and validates them). Tools: the six of HUNTING 5, the smoke bundle of HUNT_FAMILIES 3.1, the fishing rod as built, and every tool, gear item and companion of HUNT_FAMILIES 3a (#451), all proposed. Kinds: the valley's hare, carrion crow, roe deer and wolf, the elf wood's white hart, one kind for each other family whose numbers are written, and the two foxes, the canids' take before the fight (BESTIARY_LANDS 2, 3.1, 3.2, #432; HUNTING 8; BESTIARY 1; HUNT_FAMILIES 2 and 4; CREATURE_BEHAVIOUR 3 and 5.1.6, #451). A kind names its habitat tag only: its tiles are counted on content/core/map.json at every run, never typed here. A quantity 3a leaves unstated is written as 1 and says so in its note. A kind's way_tools name the tools its source names for a way (BESTIARY_LANDS: \"stalk (a sling)\", \"lure (a pit with bait)\"); an empty list is a way no ladder row serves (the bat's lantern, the spider's moth). Nothing here is content: the kinds carry no hunt block in content/core yet.",
